## Summary

When an agent has many commits ahead (e.g., +52), the Commit Status section in the agent detail panel currently shows only the first 10 commits and displays a static '+N more commits' text with no way to expand. This task adds a clickable 'Show all commits' button that fetches and displays the full commit list on demand using the existing `fetchDiffCommits()` frontend API function.

## Technical Approach

**Reuse the existing diff API**: The frontend already has `fetchDiffCommits(agentName)` in `api/diff.ts` that calls `GET /api/agents/{name}/diff/commits` and returns `DiffCommit[]`. Call this without a limit parameter to fetch all commits. No new backend work is needed.

**Type mapping**: `DiffCommit` (from diff.ts) and `LoomCommitDetail` (from types/agent.ts) are structurally different:
- `DiffCommit`: `{ hash, short_hash, subject, author, author_email, date }`
- `LoomCommitDetail`: `{ hash, message, url? }`

Map `DiffCommit` fields to `LoomCommitDetail`:
- `short_hash` → `hash` (display value), with fallback: `c.short_hash || c.hash.slice(0, 7)`
- `subject` → `message`
- `url` → `undefined` (omitted)

**Handling missing `url` field**: The existing rendering (lines 407-420 of AgentDetailPanel.tsx) already handles `url` being absent — it conditionally renders an `<a>` tag when `commit.url` is truthy, or a plain `<span>` when it's falsy. So expanded commits will render hashes as plain text `<span className={styles.commitHash}>`, which is correct since the diff API doesn't provide remote URLs. No code changes needed to handle this — the existing conditional already covers it.

**State management**: Add local component state for expanded commits and loading. Reset when the selected agent changes.

