\`buildCommand\` in \`daemon.go\` reads \`ap.assignedEpicID\` (lines 480, 493) without holding \`ap.mu\`, even though \`assignedEpicID\` is documented as mutex-protected (line 41). Currently safe because the caller (\`spawnAgent\`) is the only caller and the field is stable at call time, but fragile if another caller is added. The fix is to have \`buildCommand\` snapshot \`assignedEpicID\` under the lock before calling \`getEffectiveBackend\` (which also acquires \`ap.mu\`, preventing holding both).

## Technical Approach

Add a lock/unlock pair at the top of \`buildCommand\` to snapshot \`assignedEpicID\` before calling \`getEffectiveBackend\`. This is necessary because \`sync.Mutex\` is non-reentrant — we can't hold \`ap.mu\` across the \`getEffectiveBackend\` call. The snapshot approach (lock, read, unlock) is already the established pattern in this file (see \`getEffectiveBackend\` line 384-386, \`waitForAgent\` line 573-575).

## Files to Modify

### 1. \`internal/cli/daemon.go\`

Change \`buildCommand\` (lines 468-523) to snapshot \`assignedEpicID\` under the lock:

```go
func (d *Daemon) buildCommand(ap *AgentProcess) *exec.Cmd {
	// Snapshot mutex-protected fields before getEffectiveBackend (which also acquires ap.mu).
	ap.mu.Lock()
	epicID := ap.assignedEpicID
	ap.mu.Unlock()

	var cmd *exec.Cmd

	// Resolve backend using failover-aware resolution
	agentBackend := d.getEffectiveBackend(ap)

	if builtInRoles[ap.entry.Role] {
		args := []string{ap.entry.Role, ap.worktreePath, "--auto", "--daemon-mode"}
		if agentBackend != "" {
			args = append(args, "--backend", agentBackend)
		}
		if epicID != "" {
			args = append(args, "--parent", epicID)
		}
		cmd = exec.Command("loom", args...)
	} else {
		args := []string{"agent", ap.worktreePath, "--prompt", ap.roleConfig.PromptFile, "--auto", "--daemon-mode"}
		if ap.roleConfig.TaskFilter != "" {
			args = append(args, "--task-filter", ap.roleConfig.TaskFilter)
		}
		if agentBackend != "" {
			args = append(args, "--backend", agentBackend)
		}
		if epicID != "" {
			args = append(args, "--parent", epicID)
		}
		cmd = exec.Command("loom", args...)
	}
	// ... rest unchanged
```

Also remove the now-unnecessary comment in \`spawnAgent\` (lines 527-528) that explains why \`buildCommand\` is called before acquiring the lock — the lock concern is now handled inside \`buildCommand\` itself. Update the comment to simply say:

```go
