## Edge Cases & Error Handling

1. **Malformed URLs** — `new URL()` throws `TypeError` for invalid URLs. The try/catch returns `false`, which is the correct safe default.
2. **Relative URLs** — `/pull/42` will throw in `new URL()` (no base provided), returning `false`. This is correct since relative URLs should not be used as external hrefs.
3. **Case sensitivity** — `JavaScript:` with mixed case is handled because `URL` normalizes protocol to lowercase.
4. **URLs with /pull/ in query/fragment** — e.g., `https://evil.com/?redirect=/pull/1` — the pathname check (not full URL string check) correctly rejects these.
5. **Non-GitHub PR URLs** — URLs like `https://gitlab.com/group/project/-/merge_requests/1` won't match `/pull/` which is existing behavior (out of scope).
6. **URLs with authentication** — `https://user:pass@github.com/o/r/pull/1` — `URL` parser handles this correctly; pathname still contains `/pull/`.

