### 2. `internal/webui/frontend/src/hooks/useInlineCreate.ts`
Custom hook encapsulating the inline creation state machine.

**Signature:**
```typescript
function useInlineCreate(opts: {
  createFn: (title: string) => Promise<Issue>;
  onSuccess?: (issue: Issue) => void;
  onError?: (error: string) => void;
}): {
  isAdding: boolean;
  isSubmitting: boolean;
  error: string | null;
  startAdding: () => void;
  cancelAdding: () => void;
  submitTitle: (title: string) => Promise<void>;
}
```

**State machine:**
- idle → adding (on startAdding)
- adding → submitting (on submitTitle with non-empty title)
- submitting → idle (on success, calls onSuccess)
- submitting → adding with error (on failure, calls onError)
- adding → idle (on cancelAdding)

**Implementation:**
- `isAdding` state controls whether the input is shown
- `isSubmitting` state prevents double-submit and disables input
- `error` state shown in input, cleared on next submit attempt
- Uses `mountedRef` pattern to avoid state updates after unmount (matches useWorkspaceRepos pattern)
- `submitTitle` validates non-empty, then calls `createFn`, handles success/error

