## Edge Cases & Error Handling

1. **DiffViewer chunk fails to load (network error):** React.lazy will throw, caught by nearest error boundary. The app has no explicit error boundary around this — consider wrapping the Suspense in a try/catch error boundary. However, this matches the existing pattern (TerminalPanel in App.tsx uses Suspense without error boundary). Acceptable for now — a failed lazy load shows React's default error. Can add error boundary in a follow-up if needed.

