## Summary

This task adds a backend availability check to the \"+ backend\" dropdown used for opening new AI backend sessions. It creates a new \`GET /api/backends\` endpoint that returns each backend's health/availability status, a \`useBackends\` hook for fetching this data, and wires it into the existing \`BackendSelectorDropdown\` component (which already exists and is data-driven via props).

The key architectural element is a new \`BackendOps\` interface in the webui package, following the exact same injection pattern as \`GitOps\` and \`FileOps\` — the webui package never imports \`internal/cli\`.

## Technical Approach

**Architectural boundary (addressing review feedback):** The previous design violated the webui → cli layer boundary by importing \`cli.ListBackends()\`, \`cli.GetBackendByName()\`, and \`cli.InspectCapabilities()\` directly. This revision defines a new \`BackendOps\` interface in the webui package (in \`backendops.go\`) with a single method: \`ListBackendsHealth() ([]BackendHealth, error)\`. The concrete implementation lives in \`internal/cli/backendops_impl.go\`, imports \`webui\` types, and maps cli-internal types (\`HealthStatus\`, \`BackendMeta\`) to webui-owned \`BackendHealth\` structs. This follows the identical pattern used by \`GitOps\`/\`GitOpsImpl\` and \`FileOps\`.

**Backend (Go):**
- Define \`BackendOps\` interface + \`BackendHealth\` response struct in \`internal/webui/backendops.go\`
- Create handler in \`internal/webui/handlers_backends.go\` that accepts \`BackendOps\` as a parameter (closure injection)
- Create concrete \`BackendOpsImpl\` in \`internal/cli/backendops_impl.go\` that calls \`ListBackends()\`, \`GetBackendByName()\`, \`InspectCapabilities()\` internally and maps results to \`webui.BackendHealth\`
- Inject via \`ServerConfig.BackendOps\` → \`setupRoutes\` → handler, nil-gated like git/file ops
- Wire injection in \`internal/cli/serve.go\` alongside existing \`gitOps\` injection

**Frontend (React/TypeScript):**
- Create \`internal/webui/frontend/src/api/backends.ts\` API client module following the \`config.ts\` pattern
- Create \`internal/webui/frontend/src/hooks/useBackends.ts\` hook that fetches from \`GET /api/backends\` and merges with \`backendDefaults.ts\` via the existing \`toBackendInfo()\` function
- The existing \`BackendSelectorDropdown\` component is already complete and data-driven — it just needs to be connected to the hook at the call site

**Key decisions:**
- Single \`ListBackendsHealth()\` method on the interface — the handler doesn't need \`GetBackendByName\` or separate health checks; all logic is encapsulated in the impl
- Health checks run on each API call (they're fast — just \`exec.LookPath\` + env var check)
- webui owns the response types (\`BackendHealth\`, \`BackendsResponse\`); cli impl maps into them
- The existing \`BackendSelectorDropdown\` component and \`backendDefaults.ts\` are already built — this task just provides the backend data source

