func (d *Daemon) Stop() {
    d.shutdownOnce.Do(func() {
        close(d.shutdown)
    })
    d.concurrency.Close()  // NEW: unblock any agents waiting for concurrency slots
    for _, ap := range d.agents {
        d.stopAgent(ap)
    }
    d.wg.Wait()
}
```

**superviseAgent()** — add concurrency acquisition between step 2 (branch setup) and step 3 (spawn):
```go
// After step 2 (EnsureWorktreeBranch) succeeds, before step 3 (spawnAgent):

// 2.5. Acquire concurrency slot for role
if !d.concurrency.Acquire(ap.entry.Role, d.shutdown) {
    log.Printf("[daemon] Agent %s: shutdown during concurrency wait", ap.entry.Worktree)
    return
}
// Release slot when this iteration ends (after waitForAgent + recovery)
releaseOnce := sync.Once{}
releaseFn := func() {
    releaseOnce.Do(func() {
        d.concurrency.Release(ap.entry.Role)
    })
}
defer releaseFn() // safety net — but normally called explicitly below

// 3. Spawn subprocess
...

// 4. Wait for exit
exitCode := d.waitForAgent(ap)

// 4.5. Release concurrency slot immediately after process exits
releaseFn()
```

The sync.Once pattern ensures the slot is released exactly once, whether via the explicit call after waitForAgent or the defer on early return.

