Add a helper function to apply tool constraints:
```go
// ApplyToolConstraints configures tool allow/deny lists on a backend if it supports them.
// Returns silently if the backend doesn't implement ToolAwareBackend.
func ApplyToolConstraints(backendName string, allowed, denied []string) {
    backendMu.RLock()
    b, ok := backends[backendName]
    backendMu.RUnlock()
    if !ok {
        return
    }
    if tab, ok := b.(ToolAwareBackend); ok {
        if len(allowed) > 0 {
            tab.SetAllowedTools(allowed)
        }
        if len(denied) > 0 {
            tab.SetDeniedTools(denied)
        }
    }
}
```

Note: Since the daemon spawns subprocesses (not calling backend methods directly), the ToolAwareBackend interface will be consumed by the subprocess's backend initialization, reading from env vars. The ApplyToolConstraints helper is for in-process use (e.g., when `loom agent` starts and reads LOOM_ALLOWED_TOOLS/LOOM_DENIED_TOOLS env vars to configure its backend before invoking it).

