## Summary

The terminal onboarding modal (WelcomeBanner) re-appears every time the user enters the terminal view because dismissal state is tracked per-backend-name in a React useState Set that reinitializes from localStorage on each mount. However, the real bug is that dismissal is keyed by backendName (e.g., "claude"), meaning a user must dismiss the modal once per backend type. The expected behavior is a single global dismissal: once the user dismisses or interacts with ANY welcome banner, the onboarding is considered complete and never shows again.

Additionally, because the dismissedWelcome Set is initialized from localStorage in a useState initializer, if TerminalView remounts (e.g., due to Suspense boundaries or navigation), the Set is rebuilt correctly from localStorage. So the per-backend dismissal via localStorage actually survives remounts. The real issue is the per-backend granularity: a user who dismisses "claude" still sees the banner for "codex" or "opencode" tabs, which feels like the modal "re-appears on each view entry" when switching between different backend tabs.

## Technical Approach

Change from per-backend localStorage keys to a single global key. Instead of N keys like terminal-welcome-dismissed-claude, terminal-welcome-dismissed-codex, use one key: terminal-onboarding-dismissed = "1". When set, suppress ALL WelcomeBanners regardless of backend.

This is the simplest fix with minimal code changes. The WelcomeBanner component itself needs no changes — only the state management in TerminalView.tsx changes.

### Key Design Decisions
- **Single boolean over per-backend Set**: The original design tracked dismissal per backend so each backend could show its own intro. However, the bug report says "show once globally" — after seeing any welcome banner, the user understands the feature and doesn't need it again.
- **Keep localStorage (not sessionStorage)**: Dismissal should persist across sessions permanently, matching the bug report's requirement.
- **Backward compatibility**: On first load after the fix, read both the old per-backend keys and the new global key. If any old key exists, treat as dismissed and write the new global key. This prevents the modal from reappearing for existing users.

## Files to Modify

### 1. internal/webui/frontend/src/components/TerminalView/TerminalView.tsx
**Changes:**
- Replace the dismissedWelcome useState<Set<string>> initializer that scans localStorage for terminal-welcome-dismissed-* keys with a simple useState<boolean> that checks for a single terminal-onboarding-dismissed key
- Add backward-compat migration: if any old terminal-welcome-dismissed-* key exists in localStorage, set the new global key and remove old keys
- Replace handleDismissWelcome(backendName: string) with handleDismissWelcome() (no parameter needed)
- Update the WelcomeBanner render condition from !dismissedWelcome.has(tab.backendName) to !dismissedWelcome (simple boolean check)
- Update the onDismiss callback to call handleDismissWelcome() without backendName
- Update the onExampleClick callback similarly
- Remove dismissedWelcome from the renderTerminalPane dependency array (or keep it as the new boolean)

**Specific state change:**
```typescript
// BEFORE: per-backend Set
const [dismissedWelcome, setDismissedWelcome] = useState<Set<string>>(() => {
  const set = new Set<string>();
  try {
    for (let i = 0; i < localStorage.length; i++) {
      const key = localStorage.key(i);
      if (key?.startsWith("terminal-welcome-dismissed-")) {
        set.add(key.slice("terminal-welcome-dismissed-".length));
      }
    }
  } catch { }
  return set;
});

// AFTER: single global boolean
const [dismissedWelcome, setDismissedWelcome] = useState<boolean>(() => {
  try {
    if (localStorage.getItem("terminal-onboarding-dismissed") === "1") return true;
    // Backward compat: migrate old per-backend keys
    for (let i = 0; i < localStorage.length; i++) {
      const key = localStorage.key(i);
      if (key?.startsWith("terminal-welcome-dismissed-")) {
        localStorage.setItem("terminal-onboarding-dismissed", "1");
        return true;
      }
    }
  } catch { }
  return false;
});
```

**Specific handler change:**
```typescript
// BEFORE
const handleDismissWelcome = useCallback((backendName: string) => {
  setDismissedWelcome((prev) => { ... });
  localStorage.setItem(`terminal-welcome-dismissed-${backendName}`, "1");
}, []);

// AFTER
const handleDismissWelcome = useCallback(() => {
  setDismissedWelcome(true);
  try {
    localStorage.setItem("terminal-onboarding-dismissed", "1");
  } catch { }
}, []);
```

**Specific render change:**
```typescript
