const [tabs, setTabs] = useState<TabState[]>([]);
const [activeTabId, setActiveTabId] = useState<string>("");
const [isFullHeight, setIsFullHeight] = useState(false);
const [isSearchOpen, setIsSearchOpen] = useState(false);
const [searchTerm, setSearchTerm] = useState("");
const [isSessionPromptOpen, setIsSessionPromptOpen] = useState(false);
const instanceRefs = useRef<Map<string, TerminalInstanceHandle>>(new Map());
const initializedRef = useRef(false);
```

**Session-to-tab initialization (useEffect):**
```typescript
// Initialize tabs from hook sessions on first successful load
useEffect(() => {
  if (initializedRef.current || isLoading || sessions.length === 0) return;
  initializedRef.current = true;
  const initialTabs = sessions.map(s => ({
    id: s.name,           // use session name as tab id (unique per backend)
    label: s.label,
    sessionName: s.name,
    connectionState: "disconnected" as ConnectionState,
  }));
  setTabs(initialTabs);
  setActiveTabId(initialTabs[0].id);
}, [sessions, isLoading]);
```

Note: `id` is set to `s.name` (the session name) rather than a random UUID. Session names are unique (enforced by tmux) so they serve as stable identifiers. This simplifies session recovery — on reload, the same tab IDs map to the same sessions.

**New tab flow:**
- `handleNewTabClick`: If `tabs.length >= 8`, return early. Otherwise set `isSessionPromptOpen = true`.
- `handleSessionNameConfirm(name: string)`: Close the prompt. Check for duplicate name among existing tabs. Create new tab with `id: name, label: name, sessionName: name`. Append to tabs, set as active.
- `handleSessionPromptCancel`: Close the prompt (no-op).

**Tab management handlers (all useCallback):**
- `handleTabClose(tabId)`: If `tabs.length <= 1`, return early. Remove tab from array. If closing the active tab, select the previous tab (or next if first). Clean up ref from instanceRefs map. If search is open, clear search on new active tab.
- `handleTabChange(tabId)`: Set activeTabId.
- `handleConnectionStateChange(tabId, state)`: Functional setState to update the connectionState for the given tab.

**Search handlers (all useCallback):**
- `handleSearchToggle`: Toggle isSearchOpen. If closing, call clearSearch on active instance and clear searchTerm.
- `handleSearch(term)`: Update searchTerm, call `instanceRefs.current.get(activeTabId)?.search(term)`.
- `handleFindNext`: Call `instanceRefs.current.get(activeTabId)?.findNext()`.
- `handleFindPrevious`: Call `instanceRefs.current.get(activeTabId)?.findPrevious()`.

**Cmd+F intercept useEffect:**
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  const handler = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
    if ((e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey) && e.key === "f") {
      e.preventDefault();
      setIsSearchOpen(prev => !prev);
    }
    if (e.key === "Escape" && isSearchOpen) {
      setIsSearchOpen(false);
      instanceRefs.current.get(activeTabId)?.clearSearch();
      setSearchTerm("");
    }
  };
  document.addEventListener("keydown", handler);
  return () => document.removeEventListener("keydown", handler);
}, [isSearchOpen, activeTabId]);
```

**Tab switch re-search useEffect:**
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  if (isSearchOpen && searchTerm) {
    instanceRefs.current.get(activeTabId)?.search(searchTerm);
  }
}, [activeTabId, isSearchOpen, searchTerm]);
```

**Full-height body scroll lock useEffect:**
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  if (isFullHeight) {
    document.body.style.overflow = "hidden";
  }
  return () => { document.body.style.overflow = ""; };
}, [isFullHeight]);
```

