## Parity Test: Blocker Resolution Semantics Across All Three Go Paths

### Summary

All three Go blocker-detection paths must agree on which dependency types block work and which blocker statuses count as resolved. This task creates parity tests using a **shared JSON fixture** consumed by both CLI and WebUI test packages, ensuring identical results for the same input data across all paths. This follows the established pattern in plan_status_parity_cases.json / taskfilter_fixture_test.go.

All three paths now use AffectsReadyWork() semantics (blocks, parent-child, conditional-blocks, waits-for are blocking; all others are non-blocking). All paths require status=closed to resolve a blocker. oti7l.2 has been merged and these semantics are already in place.

