## Edge Cases & Error Handling

1. **No workspaces configured (single-repo mode):** WorkspaceTree hidden by rml7g.7's isMultiRepo guard. No drag UI rendered. The PUT endpoint returns a no-op success.

2. **Only one workspace:** Drag handles still visible but no meaningful reorder possible (only one item). Alt+Up/Down are no-ops. This is fine — no special handling needed.

3. **Workspace added after custom order set:** New workspace name won't be in WorkspaceOrder. The sort logic in buildWorkspaceInfo() puts unordered items at the end alphabetically. User can then drag to desired position.

4. **Workspace deleted from config:** The name remains in WorkspaceOrder but is silently filtered out during validation in handleWorkspaceReorder(). On next config save, the stale name is removed.

5. **Server save fails:** The optimistic UI update is rolled back — setWorkspaceOrder reverts to the previous array. No error toast needed (silent rollback matches the DraggableIssueCard pattern).

6. **Concurrent reorder requests:** Each PUT writes the full order array, so the last write wins. This is acceptable for a single-user UI.

7. **"All Workspaces" drag attempt:** The entry is rendered OUTSIDE the SortableContext, so it's not draggable. Alt+Up/Down on focused "All Workspaces" entry does nothing.

8. **Alt+Up on first workspace:** The index is 0, so moveUp is a no-op (idx <= 0 guard).

9. **Alt+Down on last workspace:** The index is length-1, so moveDown is a no-op (idx >= length-1 guard).

10. **Accessibility:** @dnd-kit provides built-in ARIA attributes for screen readers (aria-roledescription="sortable", aria-describedby with drag instructions). The KeyboardSensor supports Space to pick up, arrow keys to move, Space to drop, Escape to cancel.

11. **Config file race condition (unlikely):** Two tabs reordering simultaneously could overwrite each other. Since this is a local dev tool, this is an acceptable risk. The last save wins.

